WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.007
["A Dream Of You" playing]

00:29.071 --> 00:32.073
[song continues on speakers]

00:46.421 --> 00:48.423
[chattering indistinctly]

00:54.680 --> 00:55.681
Mmm.

00:56.306 --> 00:57.599
- [grunts]
- [Tom] Thank you.

00:58.183 --> 00:59.184
[grunts] All right.

01:00.686 --> 01:02.479
No, no, no. I got this.

01:04.022 --> 01:05.107
Hmm.

01:09.862 --> 01:10.863
See you around.

01:17.244 --> 01:18.537
Can't believe it's over.

01:19.997 --> 01:23.166
I'm gonna take Evan to a Red Sox game.

01:24.710 --> 01:25.711
Mm-hmm.

01:26.420 --> 01:27.712
Leave you with this?

01:27.713 --> 01:29.297
- Mm-hmm.
- See you later.

01:29.298 --> 01:30.299
See you later.

01:31.258 --> 01:32.259
[groans]

01:43.729 --> 01:45.355
[song ends]

01:48.192 --> 01:49.776
[Dale] Do you think it's skin cancer?

01:50.485 --> 01:52.446
Oh, yeah. Yes.

01:55.449 --> 01:57.242
[printer whirring]

01:58.744 --> 02:00.412
[phone ringing in distance]

02:03.248 --> 02:04.750
[footsteps approaching]

02:09.338 --> 02:10.339
Tom?

02:11.924 --> 02:14.050
The phone's been ringing off the hook.

02:14.051 --> 02:15.343
- Mitch called.
- Mm-hmm.

02:15.344 --> 02:18.222
Ray Mellor called. Kurt Warburton called.

02:18.972 --> 02:21.057
They've been looking for you for two days.

02:21.058 --> 02:22.351
Ruth,

02:23.101 --> 02:25.229
don't worry. Everything's fine.

02:26.939 --> 02:28.732
[intriguing music playing]

02:29.316 --> 02:30.317
[sighs]

02:58.262 --> 03:00.097
[music fades]

03:12.776 --> 03:13.777
Okay.

03:24.580 --> 03:26.582
[sighs, clicks tongue]

03:28.584 --> 03:30.418
[scoffs, sighs]

03:30.419 --> 03:33.088
[ominous music playing]

03:37.676 --> 03:39.678
[phone dialing]

03:40.220 --> 03:41.597
[line ringing]

03:42.931 --> 03:43.932
Evan?

03:44.892 --> 03:46.351
I got sandwiches!

03:50.439 --> 03:53.984
And it looks like you've got mail!

03:56.820 --> 03:58.071
[Evan] Welcome home, Tom.

03:59.239 --> 04:01.241
Hey. You were asleep this morning, I…

04:07.581 --> 04:08.916
You went through the basement?

04:13.003 --> 04:16.089
No, I went through your trunk.
What the hell is in the basement?

04:19.635 --> 04:22.094
[voice on phone] This is
the Driftwood Diner. Leave a message.

04:22.095 --> 04:23.179
[phone beeps]

04:23.180 --> 04:24.681
Hello. My name is Patricia.

04:25.265 --> 04:30.353
Um, I ordered a chicken parm
and a slice of the coconut cream pie,

04:30.354 --> 04:35.776
and I've got a turkey patty with no bun
and a single sausage link.

04:37.027 --> 04:38.778
And I don't want a refund,

04:38.779 --> 04:42.698
I just want the person
who did this to find out.

04:42.699 --> 04:44.992
And I don't want the person
who did this to get into trouble,

04:44.993 --> 04:49.288
I just… you know, I just… [sighs]
…want them to learn from it.

04:49.289 --> 04:50.581
I don't… [sighs]

04:50.582 --> 04:52.291
- Better yet, I think I--
- The mailbox is full

04:52.292 --> 04:55.002
and cannot accept any messages
at this time. Goodbye.

04:55.003 --> 04:56.463
[stutters] Great.

04:58.465 --> 04:59.715
Um… [sighs]

04:59.716 --> 05:01.677
[ominous music playing]

05:04.054 --> 05:05.055
[sighs]

05:05.556 --> 05:09.309
[Evan] I'd love to know the story
behind this heartwarming pic.

05:10.727 --> 05:13.729
- I mean, what the fuck?
- Okay. Okay.

05:13.730 --> 05:14.897
[music fades]

05:14.898 --> 05:17.192
Why did you tell me
she died during childbirth?

05:20.654 --> 05:22.030
Because she did.

05:24.575 --> 05:26.325
She was never the same
after you were born.

05:26.326 --> 05:27.578
Okay.

05:28.120 --> 05:29.121
What does that mean?

05:31.123 --> 05:34.626
She had a preeclampsia-induced stroke.

05:35.127 --> 05:37.379
And after that, she wasn't right.

05:38.589 --> 05:39.672
She wasn't right how?

05:39.673 --> 05:42.384
[Tom] It-It…
It did something to her brain.

05:43.385 --> 05:44.386
To her mind.

05:45.888 --> 05:48.098
[clicks tongue]
And it affected her behavior.

05:52.978 --> 05:55.105
She wasn't safe to be around.

05:56.440 --> 05:57.816
And so, I had…

05:59.735 --> 06:01.653
I had to commit her to The Home.

06:03.864 --> 06:05.281
What's "The Home"?

06:05.282 --> 06:08.784
It was a very nice home here on the island

06:08.785 --> 06:12.330
for people struggling with mental issues.

06:12.331 --> 06:14.749
Like an… Like a mental institution?

06:14.750 --> 06:16.376
- Like an insane asylum?
- No.

06:17.169 --> 06:20.923
[melancholic music playing]

06:21.798 --> 06:22.925
[softly] Yeah.

06:25.385 --> 06:28.847
She died two years later
of a brain aneurysm.

06:33.185 --> 06:34.937
She loved you so much.

06:42.861 --> 06:44.279
Yeah, I read the letters.

06:45.072 --> 06:46.198
[Tom sighs]

06:47.449 --> 06:48.699
[Evan] Can I read one?

06:48.700 --> 06:51.369
[ominous music playing]

06:51.370 --> 06:52.954
"Dear Evan,

06:52.955 --> 06:55.248
I need your baby hands to get the keys

06:55.249 --> 06:57.291
and your little fingers
to reach up my nose

06:57.292 --> 06:59.086
to pull the scorpion out of my brain.

06:59.586 --> 07:00.963
Watch out for that stinger.

07:01.964 --> 07:02.965
Love, your mother."

07:09.137 --> 07:10.138
That's nice.

07:11.390 --> 07:12.391
That's really nice.

07:14.434 --> 07:15.435
Another?

07:15.978 --> 07:17.103
"Dear Evan…"

07:17.104 --> 07:20.482
- ["Our Love Is Young" playing on radio]
- [muttering indistinctly]

07:22.526 --> 07:24.695
- Uh…
- [gasps] Oh, God. Oh, you…

07:25.821 --> 07:29.156
- Oh, my God. Oh, you scared me.
- [chuckles] I'm sorry. Sorry.

07:29.157 --> 07:31.577
[Gerrie] Oh, gee… [chuckles]

07:32.911 --> 07:33.912
[exhales sharply]

07:34.997 --> 07:36.164
Can we talk?

07:37.124 --> 07:38.541
Yeah. [stammers] Of course, yeah.

07:38.542 --> 07:40.210
- What is it, Wyck?
- Yeah. Right.

07:41.461 --> 07:42.546
Well… [clears throat]

07:45.090 --> 07:48.051
…there's something I've had
in my wallet for a very long time,

07:48.552 --> 07:49.553
and, uh…

07:50.762 --> 07:52.431
I think it's time I tell you why.

07:58.854 --> 08:00.314
- Oh.
- Mmm.

08:02.566 --> 08:03.733
[grunts] Remember the…

08:03.734 --> 08:05.902
- Oh, yes, I do. [chuckles]
- Yeah. [chuckles]

08:05.903 --> 08:07.905
[dust pan clattering]

08:08.947 --> 08:10.531
- [clears throat]
- [Gerrie] Hey, honey.

08:10.532 --> 08:12.826
- [sniffs] Oh, hey there, Wyck. Hey.
- Mmm.

08:13.327 --> 08:14.994
- Well, look at that.
- [Gerrie chuckles]

08:14.995 --> 08:18.581
Ha! Honey… [chuckles] …that's
your high school sweetheart, Wyck.

08:18.582 --> 08:20.833
- Yeah.
- [chuckles] You old dog.

08:20.834 --> 08:22.836
[both laughing]

08:23.629 --> 08:24.754
Yeah.

08:24.755 --> 08:27.465
- [Gerrie chuckles, sniffs]
- Well, I better get going.

08:27.466 --> 08:32.345
I got a lot of photos
I gotta give away today. [chuckles]

08:32.346 --> 08:34.764
- Oh, okay, okay.
- [Wyck chuckles]

08:34.765 --> 08:35.932
Well…

08:35.933 --> 08:36.933
Yeah.

08:39.144 --> 08:42.397
[husband] Uh, oh, mind the glass.
I might not have gotten it all.

08:45.859 --> 08:47.194
What happened here?

08:50.239 --> 08:53.658
[husband] Probably tourist kids
who heard the Boogeyman stories.

08:53.659 --> 08:55.661
[ominous music playing]

09:02.084 --> 09:04.086
[crickets chirping]

09:08.632 --> 09:11.760
[eerie music playing]

09:28.986 --> 09:31.904
- ["Caribbean Blue" playing on speakers]
- I think… leave.

09:31.905 --> 09:35.324
I'm gonna say goodbye. Disgusting.

09:35.325 --> 09:36.743
Okay. Ugh.

09:37.452 --> 09:38.871
Um… yeah.

09:39.788 --> 09:43.916
Okay. So I might need these… [muttering]

09:43.917 --> 09:45.002
Oh, um…

09:48.130 --> 09:49.131
Yeah.

10:07.274 --> 10:08.400
[exhales deeply]

10:13.322 --> 10:15.324
[car alarm honking]

10:41.767 --> 10:43.143
[alarm stops]

11:02.955 --> 11:04.790
[yawns]

11:11.630 --> 11:12.631
[sighs]

11:37.239 --> 11:38.240
[floorboards creak]

11:50.711 --> 11:52.713
[floorboards creaking]

12:14.443 --> 12:17.154
[person breathing heavily]

12:36.256 --> 12:39.259
[Patricia breathing shakily]

13:18.257 --> 13:19.258
[breathes shakily]

13:20.259 --> 13:22.135
[floorboards creak]

13:32.813 --> 13:34.815
[crickets chirping]

13:36.900 --> 13:39.111
[breathing shakily]

13:57.462 --> 13:59.464
[tense music playing]

14:08.015 --> 14:10.434
[howling in distance]

14:19.151 --> 14:21.570
[sinister music playing]

14:22.154 --> 14:24.489
[screaming]

14:42.674 --> 14:44.843
[music fades]

14:50.265 --> 14:51.266
[music resumes]

14:51.850 --> 14:54.019
[exclaims, panting]

15:03.779 --> 15:04.780
Open the door!

15:05.489 --> 15:06.490
Open the door.

15:07.366 --> 15:08.492
Open the door.

15:09.326 --> 15:10.409
I…

15:10.410 --> 15:13.121
No! Oh, God. Ah!

15:14.122 --> 15:15.666
[whimpering, panting]

15:29.638 --> 15:30.805
[music continues]

15:30.806 --> 15:31.974
[Patricia screams]

15:35.644 --> 15:36.769
Oh, God.

15:36.770 --> 15:38.772
[panting]

15:40.607 --> 15:41.608
[yells]

15:45.237 --> 15:47.990
[panting]

15:57.916 --> 15:59.710
- [Wyck] Patricia!
- [music stops]

16:02.504 --> 16:03.589
Patricia!

16:14.892 --> 16:16.767
[dramatic music playing]

16:16.768 --> 16:17.769
[yells]

16:19.021 --> 16:20.938
Help! Wyck!

16:20.939 --> 16:22.107
[groans, yells]

16:22.983 --> 16:24.776
Oh, God. Help!

16:25.652 --> 16:27.654
[yelling, panting]

16:30.365 --> 16:32.284
Help! Help!

16:33.744 --> 16:34.745
Help!

16:37.206 --> 16:41.334
[panting] Hel… Hel…

16:41.335 --> 16:42.711
Hey! Hey!

16:43.337 --> 16:45.297
Help! It's Patricia!

16:45.923 --> 16:47.674
Hey! Help!

16:48.634 --> 16:52.178
"All spring she'd worn the half-a-heart
pendant while Samuel wore the other half."

16:52.179 --> 16:53.471
- [host] What?
- You remember those?

16:53.472 --> 16:55.723
- Those little pendants?
- [host] That's your favorite part?

16:55.724 --> 16:57.058
- Whatever. I know…
- That is cute.

16:57.059 --> 16:59.018
- …I seem so cold, but I have a heart.
- That is goofy.

16:59.019 --> 17:01.229
- [screaming]
- [host] Oh, my God!

17:01.230 --> 17:02.605
- Patricia?
- [friend 1] What the fuck?

17:02.606 --> 17:03.814
[Kris] What is she doing here?

17:03.815 --> 17:05.441
[host] I know I didn't invite her
this time.

17:05.442 --> 17:06.567
- I just…
- [friend 1] What the…

17:06.568 --> 17:08.277
- Patricia, can I help you?
- [shushing]

17:08.278 --> 17:10.321
- [Kris] What are you doing?
- [host] What is going on?

17:10.906 --> 17:12.280
- [Kris] Seriously?
- [shushes]

17:12.281 --> 17:14.408
- [Kris] Excuse me. What are you doing?
- No. Shut up.

17:14.409 --> 17:16.452
- [host] Patricia--
- Shut the fuck up!

17:16.453 --> 17:18.828
- Oh, my gosh. Uh, Patricia.
- What is happening right now?

17:18.829 --> 17:19.914
- I…
- Patricia?

17:19.915 --> 17:21.875
[pants] Call the police! He's back!

17:22.459 --> 17:24.544
- Who's back?
- You know who.

17:24.545 --> 17:27.129
The Boogeyman! Call the police!

17:27.130 --> 17:28.589
- What? Okay…
- Call the police.

17:28.590 --> 17:31.301
…you have to be joking.
Are-Are you really still doing this?

17:32.010 --> 17:33.970
- The phone line is out.
- [friend 2] Oh, my God.

17:33.971 --> 17:35.847
- [friend 1] What?
- [host] Oh, that's strange.

17:35.848 --> 17:39.434
[panting] Uh… Do you have a back door?

17:40.894 --> 17:42.938
- Okay.
- Do you have a back door?

17:43.730 --> 17:46.315
- Yes, yes.
- All right, make sure it's locked. Now!

17:46.316 --> 17:48.943
- And turn off all the lights.
- No, no!

17:48.944 --> 17:50.320
Don't play her game.

17:50.821 --> 17:53.407
Don't… Everybody knows
that she lied about the calls.

17:56.368 --> 17:58.035
All right. I lied about the calls.

17:58.036 --> 17:59.370
- [friend 1 gasps]
- I knew it!

17:59.371 --> 18:00.746
- Oh, my God.
- Didn't I say it?

18:00.747 --> 18:02.331
- You said it. You said it!
- I said it.

18:02.332 --> 18:04.542
I just… I… I felt left out,

18:04.543 --> 18:06.836
I told one person, they told everyone,

18:06.837 --> 18:08.462
and… and then I had to double down.

18:08.463 --> 18:09.881
But I swear to God,

18:09.882 --> 18:13.093
he came to my house that night,
and I swear he's back.

18:14.178 --> 18:15.678
Okay. Good to know.

18:15.679 --> 18:17.346
- Bye-bye.
- Kris, I'm just telling you

18:17.347 --> 18:18.724
- so that you--
- [screams] Go away!

18:19.308 --> 18:22.102
Stop making this about you.
It's not about you!

18:23.395 --> 18:26.314
I'm sorry, but I am not the reason
that you don't have any friends.

18:26.315 --> 18:28.900
It's because you're fucking insane. Okay?

18:28.901 --> 18:30.776
Your little party?
It almost killed everyone.

18:30.777 --> 18:32.779
And now you've ruined book club.

18:33.280 --> 18:34.615
You're so annoying.

18:35.199 --> 18:37.743
Just go bye-bye, all right?

18:39.077 --> 18:40.078
Go bye-bye.

18:40.996 --> 18:42.706
Bye-bye. Okay?

18:43.749 --> 18:44.750
Bye-bye.

18:45.584 --> 18:46.959
Bye-b-- [groans]

18:46.960 --> 18:48.920
[all gasping, clamoring] Oh, my God. Kris!

18:48.921 --> 18:50.713
She's the worst! She's the fucking worst.

18:50.714 --> 18:52.340
And… [scoffs, stammers] …I'm sorry.

18:52.341 --> 18:54.259
- [host] Kris, are you okay?
- You okay?

18:55.219 --> 18:56.220
Hello?

18:56.803 --> 18:59.055
[ominous music playing]

18:59.056 --> 19:00.515
[host] Where's she going?

19:00.516 --> 19:01.767
Patricia. What?

19:02.643 --> 19:05.646
[speaking indistinctly]

19:07.814 --> 19:10.400
[friend 1] Guys, I'm gonna call 911
to report the incident here.

19:11.360 --> 19:12.694
[speaking indistinctly]

19:13.654 --> 19:15.655
[ominous music continues]

19:15.656 --> 19:17.783
[host] God. [scoffs]
I want her to get off my lawn.

19:21.620 --> 19:23.162
[Patricia panting]

19:23.163 --> 19:25.165
[speaking indistinctly]

19:29.586 --> 19:30.921
[friend 1] She's still out there?

19:37.302 --> 19:38.386
[dramatic sting plays]

19:38.387 --> 19:40.889
He's inside the house! Get…

19:41.682 --> 19:42.891
Get out of there!

19:43.892 --> 19:45.185
Get… [pants]

19:46.311 --> 19:47.812
Oh, d… [panting]

19:47.813 --> 19:49.230
He's gonna kill you!

19:49.231 --> 19:50.898
Get out of there!

19:50.899 --> 19:52.901
- [rapid footsteps]
- [music fades]

19:54.778 --> 19:57.029
- [screams] Goddamn!
- [host] What was that?

19:57.030 --> 19:59.032
[panting]

20:06.415 --> 20:07.498
[ominous music resumes]

20:07.499 --> 20:08.500
[yelps] Fuck!

20:10.961 --> 20:12.880
- [groans]
- [music intensifies]

20:19.845 --> 20:22.431
No! [grunts] No!

20:23.265 --> 20:24.974
- [horn honks]
- [tires screech]

20:24.975 --> 20:27.728
- [crashes]
- [music fades]

20:32.691 --> 20:34.109
[distorted] Can you hear me?

20:35.152 --> 20:37.988
Hey, hey. Take it easy.

20:38.906 --> 20:40.365
Looks like you hit your head.

20:40.908 --> 20:42.867
- [paramedic] I've got a pulse.
- [muttering]

20:42.868 --> 20:43.951
[paramedic] He's alive.

20:43.952 --> 20:46.621
- [ominous music resumes]
- No, no, no. [grunts]

20:46.622 --> 20:48.664
- Whoa. Whoa.
- Give me your keys. I'll run him over.

20:48.665 --> 20:49.832
- What?
- Give me your keys.

20:49.833 --> 20:51.126
I need to run him over.

20:51.668 --> 20:52.752
Welcome back, bud.

20:52.753 --> 20:54.171
Run! [grunts]

20:54.755 --> 20:55.922
[chokes]

20:55.923 --> 20:57.131
Just run!

20:57.132 --> 20:58.257
- Oh, fuck!
- Just…

20:58.258 --> 20:59.592
[menacing music playing]

20:59.593 --> 21:01.345
[breathing heavily]

21:05.432 --> 21:07.142
[choking]

21:15.192 --> 21:16.777
[breathing heavily]

21:22.866 --> 21:24.618
No! [screams]

21:26.119 --> 21:27.371
[grunts, panting]

21:28.539 --> 21:29.540
[whimpers]

21:30.415 --> 21:32.793
[music fades]

21:35.921 --> 21:36.922
"Dear Evan.

21:37.589 --> 21:40.384
Everyone has two mothers.
A mother and a secret mother.

21:41.009 --> 21:42.218
Which one am I?

21:42.219 --> 21:45.013
I am your secret mom,
and I live in a secret house.

21:46.682 --> 21:48.891
They won't let me out.
When you're a little older,

21:48.892 --> 21:51.311
you can come here
and pretend to be that awful mailman.

21:51.812 --> 21:55.190
To review, I'm dead,
I'm dead, I'm already dead.

21:55.899 --> 21:58.402
It's too late. Come soon. Mother."

22:00.612 --> 22:01.613
Sounds good.

22:11.999 --> 22:15.627
[melancholic music playing]

22:18.380 --> 22:19.631
[sighs]

22:20.841 --> 22:21.842
[sniffs]

22:27.431 --> 22:31.059
[smacks lips] This was your mother.

22:32.311 --> 22:33.312
And this.

22:39.568 --> 22:40.569
This.

22:44.114 --> 22:45.115
This.

22:50.579 --> 22:52.497
And this person

22:53.874 --> 22:56.084
wouldn't want you to remember the other.

23:03.217 --> 23:04.843
Why did you hide those from me?

23:05.511 --> 23:08.722
Oh, because they make me sadder
than I already am.

23:12.935 --> 23:14.436
I'm so sorry, Evan.

23:22.486 --> 23:24.529
Why do we never leave this island?

23:24.530 --> 23:25.531
[music fades]

23:27.491 --> 23:28.575
We can.

23:31.370 --> 23:32.996
We can leave this island.

23:43.841 --> 23:45.174
- [Evan] Sox tickets?
- Yeah.

23:45.175 --> 23:46.551
- Is this real?
- Yes, it's real.

23:46.552 --> 23:47.885
- Yeah--
- We… No.

23:47.886 --> 23:50.847
It… W-We're gonna make
a weekend of it in Boston.

23:50.848 --> 23:52.682
- This… This weekend.
- You're being serious?

23:52.683 --> 23:54.184
Yes, I'm being serious.

23:55.102 --> 23:57.645
Because things are gonna
be different from now on.

23:57.646 --> 23:59.648
[gentle music playing]

24:03.193 --> 24:04.778
[both laugh]

24:11.493 --> 24:14.454
[Patricia screaming, panting]

24:21.336 --> 24:22.754
[screams, grunts]

24:25.716 --> 24:28.218
[faint rock music playing on speakers]

24:28.844 --> 24:30.262
- How's it going?
- [clerk] Hey.

24:36.268 --> 24:38.270
[suspenseful music playing]

24:50.365 --> 24:52.491
[dramatic sting plays]

24:52.492 --> 24:54.453
[ominous music playing]

25:09.551 --> 25:10.552
Fuck.

25:15.474 --> 25:18.519
I have to eat this here.
My wife can't stand the smell. So…

25:19.811 --> 25:21.562
- [stammers] …can you give me…
- Cool.

25:21.563 --> 25:23.273
[pants] I need 20 on three.

25:24.483 --> 25:25.609
Twenty on three.

25:28.487 --> 25:29.488
[sniffs]

25:31.281 --> 25:33.283
[ominous music continues]

25:44.878 --> 25:47.338
Uh, you're not supposed
to do that. [sighs]

25:47.339 --> 25:49.549
Oh, my God.

25:49.550 --> 25:51.552
[music intensifies]

26:00.060 --> 26:01.895
[Taser crackling]

26:09.570 --> 26:11.905
- Oh!
- Oh, my God!

26:18.328 --> 26:19.872
Oh, no, no, no!

26:22.040 --> 26:23.500
[Bechir] Fucking hell.

26:28.755 --> 26:31.758
No, don't! No, you're ruining it!

26:32.759 --> 26:34.094
Oh, my… [groans]

26:36.513 --> 26:38.223
[clerk groaning, choking]

26:39.057 --> 26:40.350
[Patricia] Put him down!

26:41.226 --> 26:43.061
Good God, may I live.

26:47.399 --> 26:48.900
[choking]

26:48.901 --> 26:50.277
Drop him!

26:51.236 --> 26:52.237
[yells]

26:53.113 --> 26:55.324
- [bushes rustle]
- [body thuds]

26:58.160 --> 27:00.120
- [groaning]
- [music intensifies]

27:03.207 --> 27:05.501
[breathing heavily]

27:11.256 --> 27:14.800
- [gunshot]
- [grunts, breathing heavily]

27:14.801 --> 27:16.345
[music intensifies]

27:34.321 --> 27:35.780
[music ends]

27:35.781 --> 27:36.782
[grunts]

27:43.372 --> 27:46.375
["Caribbean Blue" playing]

28:17.155 --> 28:18.407
Is there another way out?

28:18.991 --> 28:21.285
- No.
- Okay, thank you so much.

28:35.591 --> 28:36.967
[sighs]

28:37.593 --> 28:38.594
Okay.

28:43.348 --> 28:45.267
[music fades]

29:00.616 --> 29:01.617
[Wyck sighs]

29:06.371 --> 29:09.165
[reporter] Coming up, what initially
looked like high winds is starting

29:09.166 --> 29:12.084
- to look like the storm of the century.
- [Bechir] Okay. [chuckles]

29:12.085 --> 29:13.795
No, I'm fine. I promise.

29:15.130 --> 29:18.217
It's, uh, it's just a flesh wound.

29:18.759 --> 29:21.303
He just wants me to rest
for a couple weeks.

29:22.346 --> 29:24.555
[wife] Vermont's looking better now I bet.

29:24.556 --> 29:27.642
- [Bechir laughs]
- [wife] I love you. [kisses]

29:27.643 --> 29:30.686
- [Bechir] I love you.
- [wife] I'm gonna get you another snack.

29:30.687 --> 29:31.688
[Bechir] Mmm.

29:34.024 --> 29:37.653
- [both chuckle]
- [ominous music playing]

29:43.492 --> 29:44.493
[wife] Hi.

29:49.248 --> 29:50.499
Uh, um…

29:52.251 --> 29:54.126
I didn't know Chelle was pregnant.

29:54.127 --> 29:56.588
[gasps] She is?

29:58.257 --> 29:59.633
[chuckles]

30:01.385 --> 30:02.386
Ah.

30:03.428 --> 30:07.057
I'm sorry. It's the morphine.
You know, Dr. Morgan doesn't play around.

30:08.642 --> 30:10.143
I thought she was in her 40s.

30:10.644 --> 30:12.312
[shushes]

30:12.896 --> 30:14.690
You tryna die twice tonight?

30:15.274 --> 30:16.400
Does Loftis know?

30:17.234 --> 30:18.235
Ah, no.

30:20.195 --> 30:22.614
No, I figured all that stuff
with his wife…

30:23.907 --> 30:24.908
Yeah.

30:25.909 --> 30:26.910
Patricia.

30:27.828 --> 30:29.997
What the hell did I see out there?

30:31.081 --> 30:32.457
[breathing heavily]

30:34.209 --> 30:35.210
[sniffs]

30:38.422 --> 30:39.423
[sighs]

30:41.008 --> 30:42.633
Listen to me. You have to go.

30:42.634 --> 30:44.719
No, see here.
You ain't gotta tell me twice.

30:44.720 --> 30:46.346
- I'm… [stutters, sighs]
- No.

30:46.889 --> 30:47.890
Right now.

30:50.100 --> 30:51.810
You can't have your child here.

30:57.232 --> 30:58.233
Why?

30:58.817 --> 31:01.694
- [music fades]
- Shit. Well, I'm not learning shit

31:01.695 --> 31:02.779
from any of this.

31:03.739 --> 31:06.490
You can't go to Boston
and not walk the Freedom Trail.

31:06.491 --> 31:08.910
I can't wait to go
and not walk the Freedom Trail.

31:08.911 --> 31:10.995
[sports commentator
speaking indistinctly on TV]

31:10.996 --> 31:12.663
You know what we should do
while we're there?

31:12.664 --> 31:13.665
What?

31:14.541 --> 31:16.126
Check out some colleges.

31:18.420 --> 31:19.796
- Really?
- Yes, really.

31:20.297 --> 31:22.299
- I would love… [chuckles]
- [knocks on door]

31:28.305 --> 31:30.557
[wind howling]

31:31.600 --> 31:32.851
It's not over.

31:33.560 --> 31:35.561
[ominous music playing]

31:35.562 --> 31:36.854
[sighs]

31:36.855 --> 31:37.856
[softly] No.

31:40.150 --> 31:41.317
[sighs]

31:41.318 --> 31:44.530
- [wind howling intensifies]
- [thunder rumbling]
